# Intent
Build a Rewards shelf that makes the earned-points loop legible **and makes
spending feel like it did something**. A balance ticking down with an
unchanged avatar was the original failure mode; the page now renders what the
user owns onto the companion.

# Requirements

## The avatar (top of page, the payoff)
- Render the companion (🐣) with worn accessory emoji floating above it, from
  `look.accessories`.
- When `look.themeKey` is set, apply that theme's backdrop gradient to the
  avatar panel. **Write the gradient class strings as literals in a lookup
  map** — Tailwind's scanner cannot see dynamically constructed class names,
  so building them at runtime silently ships an unstyled panel.
- Show level, mood, XP, and the active theme emoji beneath.
- When nothing is worn and no theme is active, say so plainly ("Nothing on
  yet — redeem something below and it shows up here") rather than leaving the
  panel looking broken.

## Redeem interaction
- On success, update balance, companion, `owned`, and `look` from the
  response; briefly scale the panel; bounce the just-earned emoji over the
  companion; and show "Level up!" only when `result.leveledUp` is true. Clear
  all of it after ~1.6s.
- Never fake the celebration — it fires only after a successful response, and
  a live API failure stays labeled rather than falling back to fixture data.
- Disable each button while its own redeem is in flight, and when the item is
  unaffordable (label it `Need N more`).

## Collection
- A wrap of every owned item's emoji with a count badge for repeats. Omit the
  section entirely when nothing is owned.

## Shelf
- Every item with emoji, name, description, and a `Worn` / `Backdrop` /
  `Kept` label derived from its kind, so the user knows what a purchase will
  do before spending. Mark owned items (`owned`, `owned ×N`).

# Interfaces
Use `RewardsResponse`, `Reward`, `OwnedReward`, `CompanionLook`,
`RedeemResult`, `getRewards`, `redeemReward`, and `isFixtureMode` from
`src/lib/ui-data.ts`. Do not declare a local copy of the rewards shape.

# Output
`src/app/rewards/page.tsx`

# Acceptance criteria
- Redeeming an accessory makes its emoji appear above the companion with no
  page reload.
- Redeeming a theme visibly changes the avatar panel's background.
- Level-up UI appears only when the API reports `leveledUp`.
- An empty collection omits the collection section rather than showing an
  empty row.
- Unaffordable items are disabled and state the shortfall.
- A failed redeem shows a labeled error and plays no celebration.
